{% comment %}
  Entry step — the first screen shown when the booking flow opens.
  Lets the visitor choose between "Book a consultation" and "Request a therapy session".

  Mobile and desktop have genuinely different compositions here, not just a reflow:
  on mobile the heading overlays the banner image directly and the location line
  sits at the very bottom with no eyebrow; on desktop they're separate, with an
  eyebrow and a frosted location bar. Rather than force one DOM structure to serve
  both via complex CSS repositioning, each gets its own markup below, toggled by
  breakpoint via CSS display (.kal-step-entry__mobile / .kal-step-entry__desktop).
  The option cards ARE shared between the two (via kal-booking-flow-option-card.liquid)
  since those are identical in both.

  Location line is a DUMMY placeholder for now (we're building in the demo store,
  not on a real clinic page). Once this is ported to the real theme, this should
  read from that page's clinic settings instead — see custom-clinic-consultation-form.liquid
  in the real theme export for the pattern (clinic_name / clinic_area settings).

  Banner image: ships with a default (assets/kal-booking-entry-banner.png), but a
  merchant can override it via Theme settings → Kal Booking Flow → Entry step
  banner image (image_picker setting) without touching code.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign banner_image_url = settings.kal_booking_entry_banner_image | default: nil
-%}

<div class="kal-step-entry">

  {%- comment -%} ============ MOBILE ONLY (below 750px) ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-entry__mobile">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__banner kal-step-entry__banner--mobile" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- if banner_image_url -%}
        <img
          src="{{ banner_image_url | image_url: width: 750 }}"
          alt=""
          loading="lazy"
          class="kal-step-entry__banner-image"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          src="{{ 'kal-booking-entry-banner.png' | asset_url }}"
          alt=""
          loading="lazy"
          class="kal-step-entry__banner-image"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading kal-step-entry__heading--overlay">Calm care,<br>closer than you think.</h2>
    </div>

    <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
      Book a consultation in under a minute, no account needed. Pay at the clinic when you arrive.
    </p>

    <p class="kal-step-entry__label">What would you like to do?</p>

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-option-card', variant: 'primary', icon_name: 'calendar', title: 'Book a consultation', subtitle: 'In-clinic or video under a minute', goto: 'concern-select' -%}
    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-option-card', variant: 'secondary', icon_name: 'monitor', title: 'Request a therapy session', subtitle: 'Talk to our care coordinator', goto: 'therapy-slot' -%}

    <div class="kal-step-entry__location kal-step-entry__location--mobile">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'location-pin' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        <!-- DUMMY VALUE — replace with real clinic name/area once on a real clinic page -->
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ============ DESKTOP ONLY (750px and up) ============ {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-entry__desktop">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info">
      <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Calm care, closer than you think.</h2>
        <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
          Book a consultation in under a minute in-clinic or video.
        </p>
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Entry's desktop left column swaps the shared address bar
        (.kal-step-entry__location, still used as-is by every other
        desktop step's left column — Doctor Select, Slot Picker, etc.)
        for a "Need assistance?" help line instead (node/export "Frame
        3812") — this is the very first screen, before any clinic has
        been picked, so there's no location to show yet. Own class
        (.kal-step-entry__help) rather than overloading
        .kal-step-entry__location, which every other step still depends
        on for its address bar. Phone number is a DUMMY placeholder, same
        as the mobile/desktop location text elsewhere in this step.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-step-entry__help">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
        </span>
        <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">
          Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-entry__action-panel">
      <div class="kal-step-entry__banner" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if banner_image_url -%}
          <img
            src="{{ banner_image_url | image_url: width: 936 }}"
            srcset="
              {{ banner_image_url | image_url: width: 468 }} 468w,
              {{ banner_image_url | image_url: width: 936 }} 936w"
            sizes="468px"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
            class="kal-step-entry__banner-image"
          >
        {%- else -%}
          <img
            src="{{ 'kal-booking-entry-banner.png' | asset_url }}"
            alt=""
            loading="lazy"
            class="kal-step-entry__banner-image"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- comment -%}
        Own wrapper (node/export "Container", 24px gap) around the label +
        both option cards — the export nests these one level deeper than
        the banner above, with its own 24px gap distinct from the 36px gap
        between the banner and this whole block (see
        .kal-step-entry__action-panel's own gap in the CSS). Both this
        wrapper's gap and Frame 3804's inner card-to-card gap are 24px in
        the export, so one flat 24px gap here reproduces both without
        needing the extra nesting level.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-step-entry__options">
        <p class="kal-step-entry__label">What would you like to do?</p>

        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-option-card', variant: 'primary', icon_name: 'calendar', title: 'Book a consultation', subtitle: 'In-clinic or video under a minute', goto: 'concern-select' -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-option-card', variant: 'secondary', icon_name: 'monitor', title: 'Request a therapy session', subtitle: 'Talk to our care coordinator', goto: 'therapy-slot' -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
